<title>ITALY: ITALY'S BURGO SEES 1996 NET PROFITS FALL.</title>
<headline>ITALY'S BURGO SEES 1996 NET PROFITS FALL.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian paper and packaging group Cartiere Burgo on Friday reported that its 1996 net consolidated profit fell to 100.5 billion lire from 203.4 billion lire in 1995.</p>
<p>The group added in a statement that it would pay a dividend of 400 lire per ordinary share compared to 600 lire in 1995, while its savings share dividend would fall to 500 lire from 700 lire in 1995.</p>
</text>
